# `while (!r.done) { s += r.value; r = it.next(); }`: an iteration stepped by hand. Without a sum a typed copy of this loop is weighed and refused: nothing leaves its turns. A sum among the counters counted as a test in front,
# and `counters.isEmpty()` no longer held: the loop was bought for the sum, its turns, which run other code, left the typed copy, and a list of a hundred cost 12,700 for 10,300.
# A sum changes no decision that a typed copy built for another reason hangs on; it rides along, and buys alone only where there is nothing else to weigh.
